                    correct: 1,
                    explanation: 'Productive debt: the interest rate paid is LOWER than the return generated by the funded asset. Home loan at 8.5% < property appreciation at 11% = positive spread of 2.5%. Education loan at 9% < salary increase of 80% (IRR extremely high) = extraordinary return on investment. Both create net wealth over time. In contrast, vacation loans and credit card balances fund experiences that depreciate to zero value — guaranteed wealth destruction at high rates.',
